<title>USA: Nuclear Metals gets Lockheed Martin pact.</title>
<headline>Nuclear Metals gets Lockheed Martin pact.</headline>
<dateline>CONCORD, Mass. 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nuclear Metals Inc said on Tuesday that it has received a contract from Lockheed Martin Corp to supply Beralcast components for their Advanced Threat Infrared Countermeasures program.</p>
<p>The program is a new line of missile warning and infrared countermeasures systems to be used on military aircraft, Nuclear Metals said.</p>
<p>The company said the sales potential from this contract could be $20 million annually as the system enters production. The systems are expected to be made over the next 10 to 20 years, Nuclear Metals said.</p>
</text>
